  "body": "Per https://github.com/ocapn/ocapn/issues/62#issuecomment-3403298166\n\nWe currently specify that `op:deliver` receives a `resolve-me-desc` which is a reference to a conventional resolver, with which the recipient can deliver messages to forward, reject, or settle a remote promise.\n\nWe could alternatively specify messages `op:forward`, `op:reject`, `op:settle`.\n\nWe would like to get consensus on one of these options.\n\nOrthogonally but perhaps efficiently handled in the same issue, we would like consensus on how to divide and name “forward”, “reject”, and “settle”, given that these are not cleanly separable. Particularly “settle” and “forward” can be subsumed into “resolve”, “settle” must not allow settling to a promise, “forward” must forward to a promise.",
